  m_text: 'Rizal later studied medicine because he wanted to help his mother with
    her failing eyesight. He pursued <b>ophthalmology</b>, the branch of medicine
    concerned with the eyes.


    He continued his studies in Europe, including
    at the <b>Universidad Central de Madrid</b> and later trained in ophthalmology
    under <b>Dr. Otto Becker</b> in the University of Heidelberg in Germany.


    His
    travels also allowed him to encounter different cultures, literature, and languages.
    Among these was <b>German</b>, which he learned during his time in Europe. His
    experiences abroad expanded his knowledge and influenced his later writings and
    ideas about the Philippines.'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: 2180264, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
